    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b40369b7-9c98-5db7-91cc-01feb7bad6e5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-\\sin(3x)\\cdot 3 \\\\ &=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\\\ - 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} &=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
