  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100888,
      "id": "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a",
      "title": "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "925f8b66-15ec-56f7-8a9a-a7c2d4c2d660",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=6 x e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{x}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=6\\cdot\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &=\\frac{6}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{6}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}6 x e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{6x}{e^{(6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)})/3}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{6x}{e^{2\\ln x}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{6x}{e^{\\ln(x^2)}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{6x}{x^2} \\\\ \\frac{6}{x} &=\\frac{6}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=6 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "54631c69-8f6a-5407-a914-a12efa9de23e",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
