    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "06c10fd1-f23f-5705-83c7-426bf6e78eb4",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=5 y\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=e^{5 x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=5 e^{5 x}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=e^{5 x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(e^{5 x}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=1\\cdot (5)\\,e^{5 x} \\\\ &=5 e^{5 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=e^{5 x}$ and $y\\prime=5 e^{5 x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}5 y \\\\ 5 e^{5 x} &\\overset{?}{=}5\\left(e^{5 x}\\right) \\\\ 5 e^{5 x} &=5 e^{5 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=e^{5 x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "64150e29-2ce5-5f09-a680-c8c805a8ae4f",
